customer_app: Hey team — onboarding run hitting a weird ramp. After a warmup of ~200 small requests our Node integration starts getting 429s from /v1/complete. Happens ~150 rps sustained for ~30s. Logs look like every worker is doing a preflight. Any quick mitigations?

anna_cs: Thanks for the report — sorry for the friction. Can you paste the init snippet and SDK version? Also how many workers/instances are you running?

customer_app: Using js-sdk 1.4.2, serverless with 10 workers. Init is basically:```js
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
// each worker starts and calls client.prefetch();
```

mohit_eng: This looks like a classic preflight fanout + ephemeral token churn. Two quick actions: 1) enable local token cache so workers reuse tokens (ephemeralCache:true) 2) add startup splay/jitter so they don't all preflight at once. Also add exponential backoff + random jitter on 429s. On our side we can temporarily raise your preflight window.

jenna_se: Sample backoff snippet you can add quickly:```js
async function requestWithRetry(fn){
  let backoff = 200;
  for(let i=0;i<6;i++){
    try { return await fn(); } catch(e){
      if (e.status===429) await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, backoff + Math.floor(Math.random()*backoff)));
      backoff = Math.min(10000, backoff*2);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```Also set `keepAlive: true` and `maxConnections` in the SDK so your workers reuse HTTP2 connections.

sam_platform: I see a short per-tenant preflight window limit triggering for your org — bumped your preflight quota temporarily and enabled preflight-coalescing flag for your tenant for the next 30m. Please verify and I'll extend if needed.

deploy-bot: rate-limiter policy update applied for tenant customer_app — preflight quota x3 until ts=1718081800.

customer_app: Quick update — after enabling ephemeralCache, adding a 0-7s startup splay, and the backoff snippet the 429s dropped almost completely. Huge help :raised_hands: Logs now show preflight coalesced rather than repeated:```log
[1718080012] preflight:cache hit uid=xyz token_age=12s
[1718080020] request:200 path=/v1/complete latency=150ms
```

anna_cs: Great — I'll send a short runbook with recommended SDK flags (ephemeralCache:true, preflightCoalesce:true, startupSplay=0-10s, backoff jitter), and a template to share with your infra team. Can you paste a quick after-action with final config & whether you want the quota change made permanent?

customer_app: Will do. Final config for now: workers=10, js-sdk=1.4.2 + local patches (ephemeralCache:true), startup splay 0-7s, backoff base 200ms max 10s. We'll plan to upgrade to 1.4.5 tomorrow. Thanks everyone.

mohit_eng: FYI 1.4.5 includes improved preflight coalescing and reduces per-tenant preflight cost by ~40% — ping me if you want an assist on the upgrade. :+1:
